# Pagination

Every list is server-paginated. Never return or fetch an entire collection.

## API

- Accept `page`, `pageSize`, optional `search` and `orderBy` via `PaginationQueryDto`.
- Default `page=1`, `pageSize=20`, max `pageSize=100`.
- Respond with `{ data, pagination }` where pagination has `page`, `pageSize`, `total`, `totalPages`, `hasNext`, `hasPrev`.
- Use `normalizePagination` + `buildPaginated` from `apps/api/src/common/pagination`.
- Apply `skip`/`take` and `count` on the same `where` (including role scope and search).

```ts
// BAD
return this.prisma.order.findMany({ where });

// GOOD
const { page, pageSize, skip, take } = normalizePagination(query);
const [rows, total] = await Promise.all([
  this.prisma.order.findMany({ where, skip, take, orderBy }),
  this.prisma.order.count({ where }),
]);
return buildPaginated(rows, page, pageSize, total);
```

## Frontend

- BFF only: `/api/*` with the same query string.
- `createResource.useList` returns `Paginated<T>`, never a raw array.
- List pages use `EntityListPage` or the shared `Pagination` component.
- Table search/sort/page live in `useTableState` and are sent to the API.
- Kanban/grid lists paginate each column or the grid — not by loading everything.

Reports/dashboard KPIs are not lists and do not use this contract.
